          "status": "reporter_interpretation",
          "text": "Observation — The new capability attempt ended execution-incomplete and mathematically inconclusive, with insufficient verification and no task-acceptance result. The numerical layer was unqualified because the native method requires a finite, contact-free, unconstrained state. Before that rejection, geometry recorded one floor–payload contact at time 0.23100000000000018 s, with signed distance −0.00013816094441274768 m. This is a recorded penetration/contact observation, not a certified admissible working point or a whole-route clearance result. The partial computation used 182 rollouts, 11,066 forward evaluations, 108,831 physics-step attempts/steps, and one model build; mechanics evaluations were 0. It consumed 11.262170300004072 s of recorded numerical/worker-wall time and one charged analysis. These values describe this attempt only; no score comparison or improvement claim is available."
