              }
            }
          ],
          "status": "reporter_interpretation",
          "text": "Hypotheses — One explanation is that contact at the evaluated state prevented entry into the native contact-free numerical analysis; this predicts that an otherwise admissible finite, unconstrained state would permit the numerical layer to proceed, and would be weakened if the same rejection occurred without contact or state-support defects. A competing explanation is that additional unrecorded solver-progress or state-validity problems contributed independently; it predicts further qualification failures even after the recorded contact condition is absent, and would be weakened by complete records showing contact as the sole failed prerequisite. Neither hypothesis establishes structural or global nonlinear infeasibility, because the solve was only partial and static qualification and dynamic validation were not evaluated."
